{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The 100 events are what TelemetryDeck’s SwiftSDK sends in a request. The 333,333 bytes of an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event are a third of Ingest API v3’s limit: TelemetryDeck refuses a whole request when one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s JSON is over 1,000,000 bytes as its server writes it, which may be larger than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder’s, and a third leaves room for the escapes a re-encoder commonly adds, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\u","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and four hex digits for a character outside ASCII, and a space after each ","type":"text"},{"code":":","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":",","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"larger event is left out as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError\/oversized(byteCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryDeck documents no limit on a request; its 1,000,000 bytes are the encoder’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound, the most one event may be, which keeps a request to a size a retry can send again.","type":"text"}],